// Package driver owns a module compilation and its generated files.
//
// The driver decides which files to compile and when to publish the result.
// The [frontend], [checker], and [lowering] packages handle syntax, types, and
// Go code. They do not decide which files the driver can replace.
//
// # Source and build selection
//
// TGo input controls each output. For example, service_linux_test.tgo produces
// service_tgo_linux_test.go. Compilation starts at the module root. It keeps
// dependencies, assets, and module replacements at their original paths so
// that Go selects the same build inputs as a normal build.
//
// Go tools select files by Go filenames. The driver therefore puts TGo source
// at its generated paths before it requests build metadata. Go selects
// platform files, build tags, and test packages. Nested modules and dependency
// directories remain outside the driver's output ownership.
//
// # Stage results and output ownership
//
// Reading returns an ordered source list. Selection returns Go build metadata.
// Checking returns typed packages and selected output paths. Lowering returns
// replacement contents and excluded paths. Each stage receives its input
// explicitly. Lowering builds the output before publication writes it.
//
// Compile owns rollback from the first source copy through the final Go check.
// Failure restores old generated bytes and permissions and removes new
// outputs. Success keeps the new Go files and removes excluded outputs.
// Go module metadata changes remain in either case.
//
// [frontend]: https://github.com/lucasavila00/tgo/blob/main/internal/frontend/readme.md
// [checker]: https://github.com/lucasavila00/tgo/blob/main/internal/checker/readme.md
// [lowering]: https://github.com/lucasavila00/tgo/blob/main/internal/lowering/readme.md
package driver
